== Mock Examination 2 — Questions

#mcq(1, [Which of these elements is a halogen?], [neon], [fluorine], [oxygen], [nitrogen])

#mcq(2, [The formula of aluminium oxide is], [AlO], [Al₃O₂], [AlO₃], [Al₂O₃])

#mcq(3, [Which property allows an ink to be separated by paper chromatography?], [the different solubilities of the dyes in the solvent], [the different boiling points of the dyes], [the different colours of the dyes], [the different masses of the dyes])

#mcq(4, [A sample of an oxide of copper contains 0.1 mol of copper and 0.05 mol of oxygen. Its empirical formula is], [CuO], [CuO₂], [Cu₂O], [Cu₂O₃])

#mcq(5, [The molar volume at s.t.p. corresponds to a temperature and pressure of], [298 K and 760 mmHg], [273 K and 1 mmHg], [273 K and 760 mmHg], [298 K and 1 atm])

#mcq(6, [Almost all the mass of an atom is concentrated in the], [electrons], [outer shell], [empty space], [nucleus])

#mcq(7, [Chlorine reacts with potassium bromide to give], [potassium chloride and bromine], [potassium bromide and chlorine], [potassium chlorate], [no reaction])

#mcq(8, [The formula of magnesium nitride, formed from Mg²⁺ and N³⁻, is], [MgN], [Mg₃N₂], [Mg₂N₃], [MgN₂])

#mcq(9, [Which of the following would be separated by dissolving in a suitable solvent and then filtering?], [ethanol and water], [sand and sodium chloride], [oxygen and nitrogen], [two dyes])

#mcq(10, [The number of moles of HCl in 2 dm³ of a 0.5 mol dm⁻³ solution is], [0.5 mol], [2 mol], [1 mol], [4 mol])

#mcq(11, [The number of moles of gas in 44.8 dm³ at s.t.p. is], [1 mol], [0.5 mol], [4 mol], [2 mol])

#mcq(12, [Which isotope is used to treat the thyroid gland?], [iodine-131], [carbon-14], [cobalt-60], [uranium-235])

#mcq(13, [The atomic radius of chlorine is smaller than that of sodium because], [chlorine has fewer shells], [chlorine is a gas], [chlorine has a greater nuclear charge pulling the same shell inwards], [sodium has more electrons])

#mcq(14, [The H–O–H angle in water is smaller than the H–N–H angle in ammonia because], [oxygen is heavier], [water is bent], [ammonia is a gas], [oxygen has two lone pairs, which repel more strongly than one])

#mcq(15, [Which of the following is not matter?], [light], [air], [water], [stone])

#mcq(16, [A hydrocarbon has empirical formula CH₂ and relative molecular mass 42. Its molecular formula is], [C₂H₄], [C₃H₆], [C₄H₈], [C₆H₁₂])

#mcq(17, [Two gases at the same temperature have the same], [density], [mean kinetic energy per molecule], [rate of diffusion], [molar mass])

#mcq(18, [Which statement about the nucleus is correct?], [it is negatively charged], [it contains electrons], [it is positively charged and very small compared with the atom], [it is the same size as the atom])

#mcq(19, [Which of these statements about a Group VII element is correct?], [it has seven outer electrons], [it forms 1+ ions], [it has a full outer shell], [it is a metal])

#mcq(20, [Which of these substances would you expect to be a gas at room temperature?], [silica], [graphite], [copper], [chlorine])

#mcq(21, [A solid is described as crystalline when], [it has no regular arrangement of particles], [its particles are arranged in a regular repeating pattern], [it melts over a range], [it is a mixture])

#mcq(22, [The mass of carbon dioxide produced when 10 g of CaCO₃ (M = 100) decomposes completely is], [4.4 g], [10 g], [5.6 g], [44 g])

#mcq(23, [A gas is collected over water at 20 °C. If the total pressure is 750 mmHg and the vapour pressure of water at 20 °C is 17 mmHg, the pressure of the dry gas is], [767 mmHg], [750 mmHg], [17 mmHg], [733 mmHg])

#mcq(24, [Which of these species contains 18 electrons?], [Na⁺], [Mg²⁺], [K⁺], [Cl])

#mcq(25, [Which element has the largest atomic radius?], [lithium], [rubidium], [sodium], [potassium])

#mcq(26, [Which molecule contains a co-ordinate bond?], [water], [methane], [ammonium ion], [carbon dioxide])

#mcq(27, [Which apparatus would be most suitable for obtaining the solvent from a solution without losing it?], [a filter funnel and paper], [an evaporating basin], [a separating funnel], [a liebig condenser set up for distillation])

#mcq(28, [The number of particles in 2 mol of a substance is], [1.20 × 10²⁴], [6.02 × 10²³], [3.01 × 10²³], [2.00 × 10²³])

#mcq(29, [A mixture contains 2 mol of nitrogen and 3 mol of oxygen at a total pressure of 5 atm. The partial pressure of nitrogen is], [2 atm], [3 atm], [5 atm], [1 atm])

#mcq(30, [Successive ionisation energies of an element increase because], [the atom gets heavier], [the nucleus loses protons], [the electrons repel the nucleus], [each electron is removed from an increasingly positive ion])

#mcq(31, [Which group is also called the alkali metals?], [Group II], [Group I], [Group VII], [Group 0])

#mcq(32, [An atom with 6 outer electrons is most likely to form], [one bond and two lone pairs], [four covalent bonds], [two covalent bonds], [three covalent bonds])

#mcq(33, [Which of these is a heterogeneous mixture?], [salt solution], [air], [sand and water], [ethanol and water])

#mcq(34, [The percentage by mass of carbon in methane (CH₄, M = 16) is], [25 %], [75 %], [12 %], [50 %])

#mcq(35, [A sealed rigid container of gas is cooled. The pressure falls because], [the molecules move more slowly and hit the walls less often and less hard], [the number of molecules falls], [the molecules become smaller], [the container shrinks])

#mcq(36, [The number of protons in an atom determines], [its mass number], [its number of neutrons], [its radioactivity], [its identity as an element])

#mcq(37, [Which of these is a property of a typical transition metal?], [variable oxidation state], [colourless compounds], [a full outer shell], [a low melting point])

#mcq(38, [The formula of calcium chloride is], [CaCl], [Ca₂Cl], [CaCl₂], [CaCl₃])

#mcq(39, [Which of the following changes is accompanied by absorption of heat from the surroundings?], [condensation], [melting], [freezing], [deposition])

#mcq(40, [The mass of oxygen needed to burn 0.5 mol of methane completely, CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O, is], [16 g], [64 g], [8 g], [32 g])

